# tools/al/ales_album_sheet_witness.rish -- a whole record's readable table of contents: a `format lotus-album-sheet-v1` page rendered
# from an unpacked ALES223 album, the eye's version of the album frame (ALES225).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES225.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-140635_fill-ales225-lotus-album-sheet.md
# Idiom kin: lotus/cue_sheet.rye (ALES21, the readable-render idiom) - lotus/render_album.rye (ALES223, the unpacked album this
# reads). A projection -- no new frame, no new hash.
#
# lotus/album_sheet.rye renders an unpacked album as a human-readable listing. The selftest proves: every track appears in order
# with its name and manifest fields, the wav_bytes exactly the .wav length (the listing law); the page opens with the format and
# `album <count>` lines (the header law); a zero-track album renders just the two header lines (the empty law); a too-small buffer
# refuses Overflow (the atomic law). A text render only -- no real file, no DAC, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_album_sheet_witness.rish

say "ales-album-sheet: Language EN — ALES225 draws a whole record's readable table of contents: a `format lotus-album-sheet-v1` page listing the track count and, per track, its name, preset, rate, channels, frames, and size — the eye's version of the ALES223 album frame."
say "ales-album-sheet: Style Radiant — a projection, not a round-trip, the same shape the cue sheet took: the album frame is the round-trippable artifact, the sheet is the page a keeper reads; the listing law, the header law, the empty law, and the atomic law each named and proven on metal."
say "ales-album-sheet: Lens TAME — every field bounded so the page fits a fixed buffer, a too-small buffer refused by name; siloed to lotus/, no real file, no DAC, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/album_sheet"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/album_sheet.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-album-sheet: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/album_sheet.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-album-sheet: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-album-sheet: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-album-sheet' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-album-sheet: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-album-sheet line"

say "ales-album-sheet: GREEN — a whole record now reads as a page a keeper can see at a glance, the album triad (frame · content address · table of contents) whole. The next Lotus crux names who made it — a signed carry (crypto seam) on Keaton's word."
